<!--MachineBlocks Render Target — README
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.README-->
<render:README xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:render="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation"
  xmlns:scad="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad">

  <baseType>
    core:ReadMe
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Reading entry for the MachineBlocks SCAD render target library
  </is>
  <documentation>
    @machineblocks/render-target compiles MachineBlocks BML to .scad files the
    V3 library in @machineblocks/core can render. Registry name:
    machineblocks-v3-scad.

    This library is the SSOT for target registration, the two V1 processors,
    FQN-to-module naming, imports, settings emission, assembly patterns, sets,
    the customizer, source maps, and MBOM-to-SCAD serialization. Type shapes and
    the mb_block runtime stay in @machineblocks/core.

    The target calls @blockml/block-render-engine (compile strategy for both
    V1 processors). It is browser and Node compatible.

    Start at com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.Introduction.
    For the runtime API, also read
    com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad.ScadRenderTarget in @machineblocks/core.
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:Introduction" relation="ReadFirst" />
    <see type="scad:ScadRenderTarget" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="rdoc:V1Scope" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
</render:README>
